1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Each morning, as the first rays of sunlight filtered through the trees,

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Mr. Tanaka would settle onto his favorite park bench.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
At 83, his movements were slow but deliberate, his eyes gentle and thoughtful.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
On his lap, rested a worn leather notebook, pages filled with memories and sketches,

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
and in his hand, a delicate paper crane. One of many, he had folded with quiet devotion.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The world around him bustled with life. Children dashed past, laughter echoing,

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:40,000
their games oblivious to the old man and his ritual. Yet, Mr. Tanaka remained a steadfast presence,

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:51,000
folding crane after crane, each crease a silent act of remembrance.

